<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikheil Saakashvili</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikheil Saakashvili is a Georgian politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rose-revolution">Rose Revolution</a> of 2003 and was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 2004 to 2013. His government fought corruption, rebuilt the police and sought membership of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, and his term included the 2008 war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He later served as governor of Odesa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and was imprisoned after returning to Georgia in 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikheil-saakashvili.jpg" alt="Mikheil Saakashvili" width="267" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Виталий Носач / РБК-Украина · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9C%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%B8%D0%BB_%D0%A1%D0%B0%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%88%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8_(04-10-2021)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
